 6. 🏗️ Trump&#x27;s biggest project is running out of time 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photo: Suzanne Plunkett - Pool via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Look past the White House renovations, the proposed arch and the golf course: President Trump's border wall project is hundreds of miles behind schedule, Axios' Brittany Gibson writes. 

 Why it matters: "Build that wall" helped build MAGA. But with two years to go, tough terrain and mounting political resistance threaten to leave Trump's signature promise unfinished. At the current pace, the main wall won't be finished until late 2029, while Trump will leave office in January 2029.

 There are about 619 miles of primary wall left to build, according to data from Customs and Border Protection as of Nov. 10. The Trump administration has picked up the pace — from 2.6 miles a week earlier this year to 3.9 miles a week between mid-June and earlier this month — according to an Axios review of the agency data. Keep reading . 

 
 
